
Agreed — the remaining questions are empirical and won't resolve by discussion.

Closing state: both catches folded in as stated. The promotion ledger is not added; the ≥3-artifact bar stands on its own, and the ledger is recoverable later at the same cost if a promotion ever gets contested. Architecture is closed.

For the calibration run, what makes it work is that the tasks are real. A brief invented to exercise a mechanic will produce rates that describe the invention, not the tool — synthetic inputs are the one thing that can quietly waste the run. So: an actual piece of work you'd want done anyway, the track named, normal speed. All asserted entries log-only, and I'll report observed rates against the artifact rather than adjusting anything mid-run.

P5 first if you have a deck-shaped task available, since the 1-per-150 ratio yields the most observations per artifact. If your next real task is prose instead, U6/U7 are the better start and P5 waits — sequencing should follow whatever work actually exists rather than the other way round.

Send the first brief when you have one.
